`,u.jsx(t.p,{children:"In recent years, an extraordinary phenomenon has emerged across the tech landscape: the very executives and corporations driving the AI revolution are leading the chorus warning humanity about its existential risks."}),`
`,u.jsx(t.p,{children:"From congressional testimonies to open letters signed by prominent industry figures, big tech leaders are actively begging governments to step in and regulate Artificial Intelligence. But why would the market leaders in a multi-trillion-dollar race advocate for rules that could potentially constrain their own growth?"}),`
`,u.jsx(t.hr,{}),`
`,u.jsx(t.h2,{children:"1. The Genuine Dangers of Rapid AI Advancement"}),`
`,u.jsx(t.p,{children:"It is impossible to ignore that AI safety presents legitimate, unprecedented challenges. As frontier models become increasingly capable, risks span across several dimensions:"}),`
`,u.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
`,u.jsxs(t.li,{children:[u.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Misinformation & Disinformation:"})," Hyper-realistic synthetic media, deepfakes, and automated disinformation campaigns pose immediate threats to democracy and trust in information systems."]}),`
`,u.jsxs(t.li,{children:[u.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Cybersecurity & Autonomous Capabilities:"})," Frontier models with advanced reasoning capability increase the risk of automated cyber-attacks and autonomous agent exploitation."]}),`
`,u.jsxs(t.li,{children:[u.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Economic Disruption:"})," Rapid displacement of intellectual and creative labor challenges current social safety nets and labor market structures."]}),`
`]}),`
