`,u.jsx(t.h2,{children:"2. Regulatory Capture: Building the Moat"}),`
`,u.jsxs(t.p,{children:["In economics and political science, ",u.jsx(t.strong,{children:"regulatory capture"})," occurs when a regulatory agency, created to act in the public interest, instead advances the commercial or special interests of dominant interest groups that dominate the industry."]}),`
`,u.jsx(t.p,{children:"When established tech giants push for strict licensing regimes, mandatory auditing, and high compliance thresholds for AI development, the unintended (or intended) side effect is the creation of a massive economic moat:"}),`
`,u.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
